      "description": "The eye of watches us, as nights go by, \nit gives the people everything they need.\n\nFirst comes she to bless the springs and ponds,\nThen comes she to push the tides of sea.\nThe eldest carries those departed far beyond,\nThe youngest makes our visions come to be.\nNow comes she to create a fertile earth, \nAnother to send a gust of wind or gentle breeze.\nThen comes storms and drizzle she brings forth,\nAnd she who joins the flocks of birds and trees.\n\n**Author**: Harold Gao",
